A `@sealed` decorator on its own line is the class's leading annotation, so the class's line range starts at L1 while its signature omits the decorator; its method is listed as a class member.
== args
input/decorated.ts
== file input/decorated.ts
@sealed
export class Service {
  run(): void {}
}
== stdout
input/decorated.ts (4 lines)
[L1-L4] export class Service
  [L3-L3] run(): void
== stderr
== exit 0
